\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{The odd Wick rule pairs inverse alternating entries}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{Let #{b} be a nondegenerate alternating bilinear form on a
#{2m}-dimensional space over #{\mathbb R} or #{\mathbb C}, with
image #{\Omega} as in \ref{fdip-008I}. For a nonzero top volume
#{\omega}, \ref{fdip-008J} makes #{I_\omega(e^{-\Omega})} nonzero.
The normalized functional is
##{W(f)=\frac{I_\omega(f e^{-\Omega})}{I_\omega(e^{-\Omega})}.}
Define #{b^\flat:V\to V^*} by #{b^\flat(v)(w)=b(w,v)}.
Nondegeneracy makes this an isomorphism. For linear forms
#{\lambda,\mu} put
##{C(\lambda,\mu)=\lambda\bigl((b^\flat)^{-1}\mu\bigr).}
The form is evaluated on the vector argument second. This is
the opposite slot from the symmetric form map of \ref{fdip-008N};
the alternating sign needs this order. For an ordered list
#{\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_{2r}}, set
#{C_{ab}=C(\lambda_a,\lambda_b)}. The order is the order of
insertion in the product below. It is not a choice of basis of
#{V}. For every #{r\ge0},
##{W(\lambda_1\cdots\lambda_{2r})=\operatorname{Pf}(C),}
where #{\operatorname{Pf}} is the increasing matching scalar of
\ref{fdip-00MD}. Every odd product has value zero. Repeated or
dependent factors are allowed. The inverse requires
nondegeneracy of #{b}; the statement asserts no singular
extension.}

\proof{
\p{Choose the ordered basis of \ref{fdip-00MD}, and let #{A} be
the matrix of #{b}, so #{A_{ij}=b(e_i,e_j)} and #{A^T=-A}.
In dual coordinates, #{b(w,v)=w^TAv}, so the covector
#{b^\flat(v)} has column #{Av}. Its inverse sends the column
#{\ell'} to #{A^{-1}\ell'}, and therefore
#{C(\lambda,\mu)=\ell A^{-1}(\ell')^T}. Use the reversed volume
of \ref{fdip-00MB}, so #{W} is the coordinate functional
#{W_A} below. Define the left derivative on a monomial by
##{\partial_i(\xi_{j_1}\cdots\xi_{j_s})
 =\sum_{a=1}^s(-1)^{a-1}\delta_{i,j_a}
   \xi_{j_1}\cdots\widehat{\xi_{j_a}}\cdots\xi_{j_s}.}
This respects the exterior relations. Splitting the removed
positions between two factors gives the graded product rule
##{\partial_i(fg)=(\partial_i f)g+(-1)^s f(\partial_i g)}
when #{f} is homogeneous of degree #{s}. It lowers degree,
so #{I_\xi(\partial_i h)=0} for every #{h}.}

\p{Write #{E=e^{-\frac12\xi^TA\xi}}. Differentiating its finite
series, using that its quadratic exponent is even, gives
##{\partial_iE=-\sum_jA_{ij}\xi_jE.}
For odd homogeneous #{f}, the product rule and coefficient of
the total derivative imply
##{\begin{aligned}
0&=I_\xi((\partial_i f)E+f\sum_jA_{ij}\xi_jE),\\
\sum_jA_{ij}W_A(\xi_jf)&=W_A(\partial_i f).
\end{aligned}}
The second line uses #{f\xi_j=-\xi_jf}. Multiplying by
#{A^{-1}} gives
##{W_A(\xi_kf)=\sum_i(A^{-1})_{ki}W_A(\partial_i f).}
}

\p{Apply this to #{f=\lambda_2\cdots\lambda_{2r}} and
expand #{\lambda_1}. The derivative removes its #{a}-th
listed factor with sign #{(-1)^{a-2}}, yielding
##{\begin{aligned}
W_A(\lambda_1\cdots\lambda_{2r})
 &=\sum_{a=2}^{2r}(-1)^a C_{1a}\\
 &\quad\cdot W_A(\lambda_2\cdots\widehat{\lambda_a}
                         \cdots\lambda_{2r}).
\end{aligned}}
Starting from #{W_A(1)=1}, this is exactly the
[Pfaffian recursion](fdip-008I). Odd products have odd degree,
while #{E} has only even degrees and the selected top degree
#{2m} is even; hence their integrals vanish.}
}

\p{The left derivative is contraction by the coordinate functional
#{\xi_j\mapsto\delta_{ij}}. TauCeti's
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.ExteriorAlgebra.contractLeft_ιMulti}
gives the alternating deletion formula. At zero quadratic form,
\leanref/tauceti{CliffordAlgebra.contractLeft_mul}
gives the product rule: the grade involution acts by #{(-1)^s}
in degree #{s}. These support the contraction identities;
the Berezin normalization and Wick recurrence are the direct
argument above.}

\p{In
\citet{v2, Theorem 9.11, p. 132}{etingof2024mathematical},
the increasing top order gives normalization #{\operatorname{Pf}(-A)}.
Changing the volume multiplies both numerator and normalization
by the same sign, leaving this normalized Wick rule unchanged.
\ref{fdip-00MF} records the two-generator sign check.}

\transclude{fdip-00MF}
